# p5 mcp: v0.0.16's /mcp menu with three servers -- a ready profile stdio
# server (fixture), a profile HTTP server that never answers (remote:
# `connecting` the whole run), and a project server waiting for approval
# (proj). List order: fixture, remote, then "Needs attention": proj.
# The stdio server is p5-mcp-stdio.ts, which the profile names by `@BUN@` and
# `@SCENARIOS@` (capture.sh writes both in), and xfx is given the same profile.
# `remote` is mcphttp in `hang` with a 600 s `startup_timeout_ms`, so its try
# outlasts the run on both binaries. At a refused port (`127.0.0.1:9`, until
# train 12) each try was a 10 s discover probe and its backoff 1, 2, 4, 8 s
# (era.rs `Config::FX`, runtime.rs `Retry::FX`, from fx's era.zig and
# engine.zig), so a snap within a second of a try's end read `connecting` on
# one binary and `retrying` on the other: PR #90's two regressions
# (.prd/tui-phase5/receipts/train-12/ci-mcp-timing/).
mcphttp hang
work p5-mcp-ws
fx: homefile .fx/mcp.json p5-mcp-profile.json
xfx: homefile .xfx/mcp.json p5-mcp-profile.json
wait 4
snap startup
wait 8
# The status line keeps its MCP text back while a server is still
# starting, up to 10 s (statusline.rs MCP_STARTUP_QUIET,
# menu.zig:443@481104fd), and `remote` never comes up, so
# here it is the full 10 s. The snap is the text once it is up, not a
# second count 2 s past the 10 (FLAKE-HINT4).
until shown proj is waiting for approval
snap startup-settled
type /mcp
key Enter
wait 2
snap list
type re
wait 1
snap list-filter
key C-u
wait 1
snap list-unfilter
key Enter
wait 3
snap server-fixture
key Down
wait 0.5
snap server-fixture-tool
type zzz
wait 1
snap server-fixture-nomatch
key C-u
wait 0.5
key Escape
wait 0.7
snap back-list
key Down
wait 0.5
snap list-remote
key Right
wait 2
snap server-remote
key Enter
wait 0.7
snap remove-inplace
key Right
wait 0.5
snap remove-no
key Enter
wait 0.5
snap remove-cancel
key Left
wait 0.7
snap left-back
key Down
wait 0.5
snap list-proj
key Enter
wait 2
snap server-proj
key Enter
wait 0.7
snap approve-confirm
key Escape
wait 0.5
snap approve-esc
key Down
wait 0.5
snap server-proj-reject
key Enter
wait 0.7
snap reject-inplace
type x
wait 0.5
snap reject-typed-x
key Up
wait 0.3
key Enter
wait 0.7
key Enter
wait 4
snap approved
key Escape
wait 0.7
snap list-after-approve
key Escape
wait 0.7
snap closed
wait 1
snap closed-status
type /mcp
key Enter
wait 1.5
snap reopened
key Down
wait 0.3
key Enter
wait 2
snap server-proj-ready
key Enter
wait 0.7
snap reject-inplace-ready
key Left
wait 0.3
key Enter
wait 3
snap rejected
key Escape
wait 0.7
snap list-rejected
key Down
wait 0.3
key Down
wait 0.3
key Enter
wait 1.5
key Enter
wait 0.7
key Enter
wait 3
snap removed-list
key C-c
wait 0.7
snap ctrl-c
snapfull end
home end
